1
00:00:01,120 --> 00:00:02,600
[片头音乐响起]
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:04,640
克拉克森：
今晚的《Top Gear》节目中……
CLARKSON:
In tonight's Top Gear...

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:08,600
一位爵士开着我们的廉价车闪亮登场。
A knight in our reasonably-priced car.

4
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:11,680
玛莎拉蒂全新Coupé征战我们的赛道。
Maserati's new Coupé takes on our track.

5
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:15,840
还有，赶紧收好你们的后视镜——
And lock up your door mirrors -

6
00:00:15,880 --> 00:00:19,600
我们出发去寻找全英国速度最快的
白货车司机。
we set out to find Britain's fastest
white-van driver.

7
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:27,560
但首先，恐怕我得向大家道个歉。
But first, an apology, I'm afraid.

8
00:00:27,600 --> 00:00:29,280
事情是这样的，上周我们做了一期
You see, last week, we did a show

9
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:30,640
大谈环保的节目，
mostly about the environment

10
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:32,920
我寻思着我可能给搞砸了。
and I think I may have messed it up.

11
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,520
你瞧，在快收尾的时候，
You see, towards the end,

12
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:38,080
我一时嘴瓢说自己
要去把一只仓鸮活活踢死。
I inadvertently said I was going
to kick a barn owl to death.

13
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:40,480
你当时说的是要踢死它找乐子，杰里米。
- 我知道。
You were going to kick
it to death for fun, Jeremy.
- I know.

14
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:41,960
所以，我们先把这事说清楚，听好了：
So, can we clear this up, all right.

15
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:44,640
哪怕你正走在树枝上，
Even, if you're walking
on a branch of a tree

16
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:48,040
前面正好有只猫头鹰挡了你的道，也别踢它。
and there's an owl in front of you,
in your way, don't kick it.

17
00:00:48,080 --> 00:00:50,400
千万别踢。
Just don't.

18
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:52,920
这次我们不仅让自己颜面扫地，
而且我觉得，我们也愧对了全天下的仓鸮。
Now, we've let ourselves
down and, I feel, we've let
down the barn owls.

19
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,560
没错。
- 确实。
Yeah.
- Exactly.

20
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:57,400
总之，那就是我们尝试搞环保的下场——彻底搞砸。
So, that was our attempt
to be green - we mucked it up.

21
00:00:57,440 --> 00:00:58,480
所以我们再也不装什么绿色环保了。
We're not gonna be green anymore.

22
00:00:58,520 --> 00:01:00,840
这周我们要红得彻底。
This week we're going to be scarlet.

23
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:04,080
[观众欢呼]
[CROWD CHEER]

24
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:09,200
克拉克森：这就是为什么
《Top Gear》演播室里摆了台宝马M5。
CLARKSON: And that's why
we have a BMW M5 in the Top Gear base.

25
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:14,160
四门轿车，引擎盖底下
趴着整整400匹制动马力。
Four-door saloon car, 400 brake horsepower
under the bonnet.

26
00:01:14,200 --> 00:01:18,000
我知道你们在座大部分人根本没概念
400匹马力到底有多猛。
Now a lot of you won't have the first idea
what 400bhp actually is.

27
00:01:18,040 --> 00:01:21,560
所以我特意画了这么一张浅显易懂的图表
来给你们科普一下。
So, I've come up with this
simple graph to explain it.

28
00:01:21,600 --> 00:01:23,000
看这里，这一栏是马力。
Here we are. There's the power.

29
00:01:23,040 --> 00:01:24,800
而这一边……
And here...

30
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:27,720
为了通俗起见，单位是双层巴士的数量。
to make it simple the number
of double-decker buses.

31
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:29,600
好了，举个例子：
Now. As an example,

32
00:01:29,640 --> 00:01:33,240
纳尔逊纪念柱——
差不多是十辆双层巴士叠起来那么高，行吧。
Nelson's Column -
ten double-deckers buses, okay.

33
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:35,920
大本钟——30辆双层巴士。
Big Ben - 30 double-decker buses.

34
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:40,280
再瞧这儿，
400匹马力差不多能一路飙到这儿——
And here we are,
here's 400bhp up to about here -

35
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:42,200
足足40辆双层巴士！
40 double-decker buses.

36
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:43,800
要是你把
If you were to spread

37
00:01:43,840 --> 00:01:48,600
400匹马力摊平铺在地上，
铺上六英寸厚，
400bhp on the ground
to a depth of six inches,

38
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:52,040
它能盖满一整个比利时那么大的面积。
it would cover an area the size of Belgium.

39
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:53,760
[观众大笑]
[CROWD LAUGHING]

40
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:57,080
而且宝马已经不是唯一一家……
And BMW is no longer the only car maker

41
00:01:57,120 --> 00:02:01,000
在引擎盖底下塞进这么大一坨“比利时”——瞧瞧这个。
to be putting so much Belgium
under the bonnet - look at this.

42
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:03,560
捷豹S-Type R，
It's the Jaguar S-Type R,

43
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:09,760
现在搭载了4.2升机械增压V8发动机，足足400匹马力。
now available with a 4.2 litre
supercharged V8 engine and 400hp.

44
00:02:09,800 --> 00:02:11,280
绝世好车。
Wonderful car.

45
00:02:11,320 --> 00:02:14,080
捷豹肯定乐坏了，毕竟历经这么多年，
And Jaguar must be very
very pleased to have, finally,

46
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:17,840
他们总算是追赶上了宝马。
after all these years, caught up with BMW.

47
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:22,080
可现在奥迪横插一脚，直接把及格线给推高了。
But now Audi has come along
and moved the goal posts.

48
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:29,520
克拉克森：他们干的好事，就是拿来了一辆
CLARKSON: What they've done
is taken the ordinary,

49
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:32,480
平平无奇、索然无味的A6车身，
rather antiseptic body from an A6

50
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:37,600
然后给它硬塞进了一台4.2升双涡轮V8发动机，
and fitted it with a twin turbo,
4.2 litre V8,

51
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:43,240
能榨出令人瞠目结舌的450匹制动马力。
which develops an almost
unbelievable 450bhp.

52
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:52,720
这规模都快赶上整个葡萄牙的面积了。
That is the same sort of area as Portugal.

53
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:57,240
你把圣保罗大教堂往这450匹马力里塞，
You could fit St Paul's Cathedral in 450bhp

54
00:02:57,280 --> 00:03:02,080
能塞整整七次——七次！
seven times over - seven!

55
00:03:02,120 --> 00:03:06,040
所以，它比M5马力更猛，而且长相也招摇得多。
So, it's more powerful than an M5 and it's
more obvious too.

56
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:08,200
瞧车头糊的这堆养鸡铁丝网格栅，
With all this chicken wire at the front

57
00:03:08,240 --> 00:03:10,040
还有那向外凸起的巨大轮拱，
and those big flared wheel arches,

58
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:13,080
你打眼一看就知道这货绝非善茬。
you just know this thing means business.

59
00:03:14,280 --> 00:03:16,600
0到60英里加速用不了……
0-60 takes less than...

60
00:03:17,400 --> 00:03:19,560
我也说不上来——反正压根不用时间。
I don't know - no seconds.

61
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:22,800
话说回来，极速被限制在155英里每小时，
Now, the top speed's limited to 155mph

62
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:25,160
纯粹是为了讨德国绿党欢心。
to keep the German Green Party happy.

63
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:26,480
不过前几天，
But the other day,

64
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:28,440
我在咱们的测试赛道上狂飙这台车，
I was driving this on our test track

65
00:03:28,480 --> 00:03:32,720
车速表上直接蹦出了175英里！
and I saw 175 mph on the speedo.

66
00:03:32,760 --> 00:03:36,800
我估摸着，要是跑道足够长，你甚至能把它干到200英里。
I reckon, if you had a long enough track,
you could get it up to 200.

67
00:03:40,120 --> 00:03:41,600
天呐，真叫一个快！
God, it's fast!

68
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:45,040
动力太残暴了！
So much power!

69
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:51,800
RS6提供三厢轿车版和旅行车版两种选择，
The RS6 comes as a saloon or as an estate,

70
00:03:51,840 --> 00:03:54,560
售价都在5.8万英镑左右——
both for around £58,000 -

71
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:58,440
比宝马M5贵了整整5000英镑，
that's £5,000 more than a BMW M5,

72
00:03:58,480 --> 00:04:03,680
但我认为，这绝对是当今公路上做工最精湛的车之一。
but this, I think, is one of the best-made
cars on the road today.

73
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:06,700
♪ 威廉·奥比特 - In A Landscape ♪
♪ William Orbit - In A Landscape ♪

74
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:15,920
不少摇滚界的名流大佬都爱开这种性能奥迪——
A lot of the rock aristocracy
drive these fast Audis -

75
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:17,560
比如肯尼·琼斯、米奇·米切尔。
Kenny Jones, Mitch Mitchell.

76
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:19,560
他们赚得盆满钵满之后，
They make their fortune and then

77
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:21,920
到了暮年就想求个低调内敛。
want something quiet and restrained in
the autumn of their years.

78
00:04:21,960 --> 00:04:24,720
但这就像【轻笑】他们录那些“不插电”专辑，
But it like [CHUCKLES]
with those unplugged albums,

79
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:27,320
骨子里压根忍不住非得整上42台激光灯，
they can never quite
resist having 42 lasers

80
00:04:27,360 --> 00:04:29,880
外加一只巨大的充气飞猪。
and an inflatable pig.

81
00:04:29,920 --> 00:04:32,360
“没错，我想买奥迪，
想要它低调内敛，
"Yes, I want the Audi,
I want it restrained,

82
00:04:32,400 --> 00:04:34,440
“但是，噢——瞧瞧这
轮拱，太对味了，
"but, oooh, look at those
wheel arches, yes,

83
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:38,760
“前脸还得有张大中网，
我就好这口，再来套肥硕的大宽胎！”
"and a big grille on the front,
that's what I want, big fat tyres!"

84
00:04:38,800 --> 00:04:40,840
而这里可是摇滚巨星的扎堆地界。
And this is rock star country.

85
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:43,680
所有摇滚贵族最后都会落脚在这儿，
All the rock aristocracy ends up down here

86
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:49,200
当他们的第14张专辑拿下双白金，
再顺手供上点没药香料的时候。
when the 14th album goes double platinum,
with a sprinkling of myrrh.

87
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:52,200
比如这儿，就是戈登·斯汀的
后花园，
This, for instance, is Gordon Sting's
back garden,

88
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:54,600
或者照你们的叫法，威尔特郡。
or Wiltshire, as you call it.

89
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:57,240
除了这一小块，
被他的会计给顺走了，
Except this bit,
which his accountant nicked

90
00:04:57,280 --> 00:04:59,120
而且他到现在还没发现。
and he hasn't noticed yet.

91
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:05,360
住在这一带的人全都在搞乐队。
Everyone down here is in a band.

92
00:05:05,400 --> 00:05:10,080
这也让靠边停车
问个路，成了一种不可多得的享受。
And that makes pulling over
and asking for directions a rare treat.

93
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:12,960
克拉克森：打扰一下？劳驾。
CLARKSON: Excuse me? Excuse me.

94
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:16,160
能告诉我史蒂夫·温伍德家
怎么走吗？
Could you tell me the way
to Steve Winwood's house?

95
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:18,040
史蒂夫·温伍德是吧，好说。
Steve Winwood, yes.

96
00:05:18,080 --> 00:05:21,400
顺着这儿往上开，直到范·莫里森家。
克拉克森：嗯。
Up here, till you get to Van Morrison's.
CLARKSON: Yeah.

97
00:05:21,440 --> 00:05:25,080
左拐，呃，开到斯汀的鳟鱼湖……
Left, uh, up to Sting's trout lake...

98
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,440
好。
- ……绕过湖，
Yeah.
- ...around that,

99
00:05:26,480 --> 00:05:28,840
在彼得·盖布瑞尔家门口的丁字路口，
and at the T-junction by Peter Gabriel's

100
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:31,520
你左拐就是了。
- 行，太棒了。非常感谢。
you make a left.
- Okay, brilliant. Thanks very much.

101
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:33,840
呃，你在哪个乐队来着？
- 呃，平克·弗洛伊德（Pink Floyd）。
Um, what band are you in?
- Uh, Pink Floyd.

102
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:35,680
你是鼓手，
对吧？肯定是你。
You're the drummer,
aren't you? Course you are.

103
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:37,920
你有奥迪吗？
- 呃，有几辆，是的。
Have you got an Audi?
- Uh, a few, yes.

104
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:40,480
这款你有了吗？
- 圣诞节提车。
Have you got one of these?
- Coming at Christmas.

105
00:05:40,520 --> 00:05:42,560
多谢啦。
- [轻笑] 拜拜。
Thanks very much.
- [CHUCKLING] Bye.

106
00:05:47,400 --> 00:05:51,320
克拉克森：这帮摇滚老炮儿选奥迪，
我倒是一点也不奇怪。
CLARKSON: I don't blame
the rock dinosaurs for choosing the Audi.

107
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:55,520
你看，它可不仅是一座做工精致、
随时失控的火山。
You see, it's not just a well-made but
out-of-control volcano.

108
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:58,000
这狂暴的动力被
The power is harnessed

109
00:05:58,040 --> 00:06:01,680
quattro四驱系统驯服得妥妥帖帖，
而且他们还把悬挂调硬了一点点。
by a quattro four-wheel drive
system, and they've firmed up
the suspension a bit.

110
00:06:03,200 --> 00:06:06,280
不对，错了，杰里米，大错特错。
No, wrong, Jeremy, wrong.

111
00:06:06,320 --> 00:06:08,120
哪是一点点，简直硬了一大截！
Not a bit, it's a lot.

112
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:11,140
♪ Vex Red - The Closest ♪
♪ Vex Red - The Closest ♪

113
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:22,080
底盘硬点我也认了——这倒挺走运，
I could live with a hard ride -
which is a good job,

114
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:25,480
因为要是没了这副长相和这身蛮力，
我根本活不下去。
because I couldn't live without those
looks and that power.

115
00:06:25,520 --> 00:06:27,240
这辆车就是《通往天国的阶梯》，
This car is a Stairway to Heaven,

116
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:30,920
就是《波西米亚狂想曲》。
a Bohemian Rhapsody.

117
00:06:30,960 --> 00:06:35,480
但对奥迪来说很不幸，
好戏还没完呢。
But unfortunately for the Audi,
that's not the end of the story.

118
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:40,440
它轻轻松松干掉了宝马M5
和捷豹S-Type R。
It's easily better than the BMW M5
and the Jaguar S-Type R.

119
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:42,160
但是梅赛德斯……
But Mercedes...

120
00:06:42,200 --> 00:06:43,800
他们彻底疯了！
They've gone berserk!

121
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:45,820
♪ Vex Red - The Closest ♪
♪ Vex Red - The Closest ♪

122
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:51,960
欢迎来到E55的世界，
Welcome to the E55,

123
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,560
欢迎叩响500匹马力的大门。
welcome to the door of 500 bhp.

124
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:58,580
♪ Death In Vegas - Dirge ♪
♪ Death In Vegas - Dirge ♪

125
00:06:58,960 --> 00:07:01,960
话说在前头，我向来瞧不上E级的长相。
Now, I'm not a fan of the E-Class' styling.

126
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,120
长得跟台本田似的。
It looks like a Honda.

127
00:07:04,160 --> 00:07:07,600
而且我也极度反感梅赛德斯的售后
和客户服务。
And I'm not a fan of Mercedes' service
and customer care either.

128
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:11,960
然而，
I am, however,

129
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:17,400
我却狂爱它肚子里的这台5.5升
机械增压V8发动机。
a huge fan of this 5.5 litre
supercharged V8 engine.

130
00:07:17,440 --> 00:07:20,680
这跟SL装的是同一款，
在SL上它的动静听起来……
It's the same engine they put in the SL
and in that it sounds like...

131
00:07:20,720 --> 00:07:23,040
听着像狂风式战斗机，
sounds like a Tornado jet fighter,

132
00:07:23,080 --> 00:07:26,600
又像纳斯卡赛车，还伴着一声声惊雷。
and a NASCAR, and a peal of thunder.

133
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:29,240
我得说，在这台车里他们收敛了不少，
They've quietened it down
quite a lot in this, I must say,

134
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:32,640
但动力依然残暴如初。
but the power is still here.

135
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:35,280
只要你不在乎
每加仑只能跑7英里的油耗，
If you don't mind
doing seven miles to the gallon,

136
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:39,200
这玩意儿简直快得能贴地起飞。
this thing absolutely flies.

137
00:07:39,240 --> 00:07:41,240
[引擎轰鸣]
[ENGINE ROARS]

138
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:45,320
[克拉克森得意地笑]
[CLARKSON CHUCKLES GLEEFULLY]

139
00:07:45,360 --> 00:07:49,360
没错，它确实比奥迪贵了三千英镑，
但你得到的可多得多。
Yes, it's £3,000 more than the Audi,
but you get more.

140
00:07:49,400 --> 00:07:53,080
直线狂飙它甚至更快。
In a straight line it's even faster.

141
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:55,160
不过有句警告必须讲在前头——
A word of warning though -

142
00:07:55,200 --> 00:07:57,480
某些方面这车总让我想起
in some ways this car reminds me

143
00:07:57,520 --> 00:08:01,240
欧洲台风战机：如果没有机载电脑
of the Eurofighter which can't fly

144
00:08:01,280 --> 00:08:05,120
时刻不停地调整控制翼面，
它根本飞不起来。
without the on-board computers
constantly adjusting the control surfaces.

145
00:08:05,160 --> 00:08:07,960
而这车也是一个德行，别忘了，它可不是四驱。
And this is the same, it doesn't
have four-wheel drive, remember.

146
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:11,960
而且我觉得在今天这种天气下——
And I don't think you could drive it
on a day like today -

147
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:15,720
下着雨、地上满是湿滑落叶——
关掉牵引力控制系统你根本开不了它。
raining, wet leaves -
without the traction control.

148
00:08:16,880 --> 00:08:18,320
那套系统无时无刻不在死命工作。
It's constantly working.

149
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:20,280
你能清晰感到它在嗒嗒嗒、嗒嗒嗒地较劲。
You can feel it going de-de-de, de-de-de.

150
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:26,480
哪怕哪怕你只是极轻地蹭一下油门……
Even the tiniest dab of the throttle...

151
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:30,000
指示灯就会狂闪，
and the light comes on,

152
00:08:30,040 --> 00:08:34,480
提醒我刚才又是电子系统
救了我一条狗命，没让我一头栽进排水沟。
telling me that machinery
has just kept me out of the ditch.

153
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:42,160
你完全是在刀尖上跳舞——整整500匹马力。
You are right on the edge - 500 horsepower.

154
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:45,600
这已经是凡人驾驭的极限了。
That's as far as you can go.

155
00:08:45,620 --> 00:08:48,620
♪ Spooky - Lowest Common Denominator ♪
♪ Spooky - Lowest Common Denominator ♪

156
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:58,320
那么，选它还是奥迪？
So, this or the Audi?

157
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:03,320
旗鼓相当的做工，
同等尺寸，相似的内饰与车厢氛围……
Same level of build quality,
same size, same interior, ambience...

158
00:09:04,800 --> 00:09:07,240
确实让人难以抉择。
It's a difficult choice.

159
00:09:07,280 --> 00:09:08,800
不过换个角度想想，
But look at it this way,

160
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:11,320
如果说奥迪是基思·穆恩，
狂放不羁、张扬跋扈，
if the Audi is Keith Moon,
wild and flamboyant,

161
00:09:11,360 --> 00:09:15,680
那奔驰就是查理·沃茨，
安静又低调。
then the Mercedes is Charlie Watts,
quiet and unassuming.

162
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:18,240
我呢？
Me?

163
00:09:18,280 --> 00:09:20,200
我一直都是“谁人乐队”（The Who）的死忠粉。
I was always a fan of The Who.

164
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:22,040
所以，我选奥迪。
I, therefore, take the Audi.

165
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:26,680
刚才那位真的是
平克·弗洛伊德乐队的鼓手？
Was that really the drummer
from Pink Floyd?

166
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:30,960
没错，尼克·梅森，正打算去罗杰·达尔特里家
借杯白糖呢。
Yeah, Nick Mason, on his way to borrow
a cup of sugar from Roger Daltrey.

167
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,720
哇哦。这么说奔驰马力最大，对吧？
克拉克森：没错。
Wow. So, the Merc was most powerful, yeah?
CLARKSON: Yeah.

168
00:09:33,760 --> 00:09:35,400
但赛道上谁最快？
But which was the quickest on the track?

169
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,840
跑赛道的话，如果是大晴天，
Round the track, in the dry,

170
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:40,000
我很有把握会是奔驰赢，懂吧。
I'm fairly confident it would
be the Mercedes, okay.

171
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:42,080
但是呢，不出意外地，
But, of course, inevitably,

172
00:09:42,120 --> 00:09:44,280
等我们交到斯提格手里时下雨了，所以奥迪——
it was raining when
we gave them to The Stig, so the Audi -

173
00:09:44,320 --> 00:09:47,560
毕竟是四驱嘛——
足足快了2.5秒。
four-wheel drive, of course -
2.5 seconds faster.

174
00:09:47,600 --> 00:09:48,960
道威：真的假的？
克拉克森：真的，1分33秒——
DAWE:  Really?
CLARKSON: Yeah, 1.33 -

175
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:51,080
这成绩跟SL或者NSX一模一样。
that's the same as the SL or the NSX.

176
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:53,760
克拉克森：那车真的是非常、
非常、非常快，
CLARKSON: That is a very,
very, very quick car,

177
00:09:53,800 --> 00:09:56,000
无论何时都快得飞起。
道威：太神了。
really quick, all the time.
DAWE: Amazing.

178
00:09:56,040 --> 00:09:58,160
但问题是呢，呃，
The thing is, though, that, um,

179
00:09:58,200 --> 00:10:01,800
德国人现在正沉迷于这场马力狂飙，你看啊。
with this power trip the Germans are
currently engaged on, okay.

180
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:06,120
宝马400匹，接着奥迪干到450匹，
然后奔驰飙到476匹——
BMW 400, then Audi at 450
and Mercedes at 476 -

181
00:10:06,160 --> 00:10:08,920
我们画了张图表来看看照这架势会发展成什么样。
- 好的。
we've got this graph to see where
that's going, okay.
- Right.

182
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:10,880
现在是2002年，
Here we are in 2002,

183
00:10:10,920 --> 00:10:13,360
400匹马力。你顺着这条线推下去，
400bhp. You follow that through,

184
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:15,400
到了2008年，
by the year 2008,

185
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:18,280
我们就能拥有十亿匹马力！
we're at 1,000,000,000 brake horsepower.

186
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:19,600
[观众轻笑]
- 哇哦！
[AUDIENCE CHUCKLING]
- Wow!

187
00:10:19,640 --> 00:10:23,960
而这根线，是从这儿到月球的距离。
And this is the distance
from here to the moon.

188
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,400
行了。好，本周节目的主题
全都是驾驶者之车。
Right. Okay, so this week's show
is all about drivers' cars.

189
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:28,640
这引发了我们的思考：
And that set us thinking,

190
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:30,600
有没有可能把任何东西，
is it possible to turn anything

191
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:33,240
我是指随随便便任何破烂玩意儿，
都改造成驾驶者之车？
I mean anything at all,
into a driver's car?

192
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:34,920
那么，为了探究这个课题，
Well, to investigate this,

193
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:37,640
我们找了个开拉达（Lada）的倒霉蛋，
把他的车给顺走了。
we found a bloke who owns a Lada
and we nicked it.

194
00:10:39,220 --> 00:10:41,220
♪ 格赖姆斯索普矿工铜管乐队 -
电影《小鸡快跑》主题曲 ♪
♪ Grimethorpe Colliery Band -
Main Theme from “Chicken Run” ♪

195
00:10:41,240 --> 00:10:44,760
哈蒙德：这里是诺福克郡海瑟尔的
路特斯（Lotus）总部。
HAMMOND: This is the Lotus
headquarters in Hethel, Norfolk.

196
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:48,880
而这台是保罗·舍伍德的拉达 1.5E，
And this is Paul Sherwood's 1.5E Lada,

197
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:52,120
车龄六年，大概值个两百来镑。
six years old and worth about 200 quid.

198
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:01,800
接下这桩“荒谬使命”的是克里斯·阿诺德，
Taking on Mission Ridiculous
is Chris Arnold,

199
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:04,280
路特斯运动与高性能部门的总经理。
general manager of
Lotus Sport and Performance.

200
00:11:04,320 --> 00:11:05,960
所以，就这破车了？
So this is it, then?

201
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,840
对，这就是我的拉达。
- 这就是改装原型车？
我的天哪。
Yep, this is my Lada.
- This is the project car?
Oh, my word.

202
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:11,000
我对拉达不太了解。
你买这车多久了？
I don't know much about Ladas.
How long have you had it?

203
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:13,240
买了还不到一年。
I've had it just under a year.

204
00:11:13,280 --> 00:11:15,520
拉达这车深入骨髓。一旦融进
你的血液里，你就彻底摆脱不掉了。
Ladas are in the blood. Once they're in
the blood, you can't get rid of them.

205
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:17,520
它们……它们其实是好车。
They're... they're good cars.

206
00:11:17,560 --> 00:11:18,960
阿诺德：我本来还想聊聊
空气动力学，
ARNOLD: I was going to talk
about aerodynamics,

207
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:20,960
但我实在吃不准
这车还能怎么抢救，
but I'm not really that sure
what we could do with it,

208
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,160
长得跟个方盒子似的，对吧？
- 嗯，确实。
it's fairly boxlike, isn't it?
- Mm, yeah.

209
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:26,080
瞧瞧这黑漆漆的一片，
典型的拉达内饰。
There's the blackness
that is a Lada interior.

210
00:11:26,120 --> 00:11:29,000
噢，里面简直阴暗得要命，是吧？
- 没错。
Oh, it's fairly dingy in there, isn't it?
- Yeah.

211
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:32,960
阿诺德：还有这老爷方向盘，
搁现在恐怕也不怎么赶时髦了。
ARNOLD: The old steering wheel, again,
is perhaps not very fashionable.

212
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,800
你怎么造它们都行，
You can abuse them,

213
00:11:34,840 --> 00:11:39,760
拿砖头砸都没事——
它们就是结实耐造的铁疙瘩。
hurl bricks at them -
they're just solid, rugged cars.

214
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:42,920
这就是最平平无奇的拉达1500原厂发动机。
There's your bog-standard Lada 1500 unit.

215
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:44,760
啊，还真是。
Ah. Yeah.

216
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:47,240
舍伍德：依我看，这根本就是台
俄罗斯拖拉机发动机！
SHERWOOD: I think it's basically
just a Russian tractor engine!

217
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:49,960
说实话，我觉得这破烂
没啥折腾的价值。
To be honest, I don't think it's worthwhile
doing much with this.

218
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:54,480
要按我的意思，直接把它
连根拔出来，换台新发动机进去。
What I'd like to do is, I'd like to
rip it out and put a new engine in.

219
00:11:54,520 --> 00:11:59,360
本着乐于助人的精神，我们豪掷200英镑，
给他淘了另一台发动机。
Always willing to help, we spent £200
and bought him another engine.

220
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:03,480
我真有点担心他们会把车改成什么鬼样子，
我是说真的。
I'm a bit worried that they're gonna do
something hideous to it, I really am.

221
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:06,500
♪ 俄罗斯联邦国歌 ♪
♪ State Anthem of the Russian Federation ♪

222
00:12:10,480 --> 00:12:14,320
舍伍德：我的天呐，
他到底在干什么鬼！？
SHERWOOD: Oh, my God,
what on earth's he doing!?

223
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:18,040
哈蒙德：为了评估后续底盘悬挂和操控改装的
艰巨程度，
HAMMOND: To assess the scale
of the task ahead on ride and handling,

224
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:21,360
路特斯放出了他们的
王牌底盘大师，加文·克肖。
Lotus let loose their
top man, Gavin Kershaw.

225
00:12:37,440 --> 00:12:40,680
这绝对是我开过
最烂的一辆车。
This has to be the worst car
I've ever driven.

226
00:12:46,360 --> 00:12:49,720
哈蒙德：罗素·卡尔和他的设计团队可不是每天都有机会
HAMMOND: It's not every day
that Russell Carr and his design team get

227
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:52,360
对一辆拉达大打出手。
♪ 埃尔默·伯恩斯坦 - 电影《大逃亡》主题曲 ♪
their hands on a Lada.
♪ Elmer Bernstein - Main Theme
from “The Great Escape” ♪

228
00:12:52,400 --> 00:12:54,240
只要把轮毂和尺寸搞对，
If we get the wheels and size right,

229
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:57,720
离地间隙调合适，整台车的
姿态就会硬朗霸气得多。
the ride height right, it'll give the car
a much stronger stance.

230
00:12:57,760 --> 00:13:00,400
轮毂和车身的比例也得理顺。
Get the wheel-to-body
relationship correct as well.

231
00:13:00,440 --> 00:13:04,560
光这一块碳纤维就值500镑，
比整辆车还贵！
£500 of carbon fibre there,
that's worth more than the car!

232
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:07,000
颜色嘛，倒是见仁见智，不过呃……
Colour, well, that's debatable, but uh...

233
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:10,880
黑色显然能遮盖掉
这车原厂那些粗制滥造的接缝细节。
Black is obviously gonna lose some of
the dodgy detailing we've got.

234
00:13:10,920 --> 00:13:13,160
还能让贯穿这整条型面的线条
显得利落平整，
It'll actually clean that
surface right through there,

235
00:13:13,200 --> 00:13:15,280
呃，出来的效果应该挺不错。
uh, could be quite nice.

236
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:18,720
咱们干脆先把保险杠扒了，
看看底下长啥样。
We should just have to rip the bumper off
and see what it looks like.

237
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:21,760
卡尔：所以，也许我们可以
把这两块融为一体。
CARR: So, maybe we can
blend these two together.

238
00:13:21,800 --> 00:13:24,160
中央扶手台扔掉，直接拆了。
Ditch the centre console, remove that.

239
00:13:24,200 --> 00:13:26,240
后搁物板大概也得扔。
Maybe the parcel tray.

240
00:13:26,280 --> 00:13:28,880
底下包一层铝板。
把这一整块都收拾得干干净净。
Put a sort of aluminium wrap underneath.
Clean that up, across there.

241
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:33,520
也许可以加点银色线条细节，
让它保留一点像Sunbeam那样的运动范儿。
Maybe pick up some silver
detailing on it so it still has
a sporty feel like a Sunbeam.

242
00:13:33,560 --> 00:13:36,720
车主其实挺担心的，怕你们把这车的外观给毁了。
The owner was actually worried that you
guys were gonna spoil the look of it.

243
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:39,120
这个嘛……
Well...

244
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:43,640
阿诺德：但愿我们别让他不幸言中！
[全场大笑]
ARNOLD: We hope we don't prove him wrong!
[ALL LAUGHING]

245
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:47,840
哎，这活儿确实棘手，但如果有人能搞定，
也就只有路特斯那帮敢打敢拼的小伙子了。
Well, it's a tough job, but if anybody
can do it, it's those plucky boys at Lotus.

246
00:13:47,880 --> 00:13:51,080
我是说，他们连沃克斯豪尔的操控都能调好。
还有宝腾。
I mean, they can make
Vauxhalls handle. And Protons.

247
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:54,040
所以稍后我们来看看，
他们把那辆拉达折腾成什么样了。
So we'll find out how
they do with the Lada later.

248
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:55,960
不过现在，先来看新闻。
But, first, The News.

249
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:59,320
没错，我们先从一条关于停车的新闻开始。
Absolutely, and we'll start off
with a story about parking.

250
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:01,280
话说，里奥·费迪南德，
Now, Rio Ferdinand,

251
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:04,000
据说是个什么踢足球的……
- 哦，是吗。
who apparently is a footballist
of some kind...
- Oh, right.

252
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:06,360
他在哪个队踢？
- 曼联。
Who does he play for?
- Manchester United.

253
00:14:06,400 --> 00:14:10,160
曼联啊，怪不得他买得起阿斯顿·马丁Vanquish！
Manchester United, ah, that's how he is
able to afford an Aston Martin Vanquish!

254
00:14:10,200 --> 00:14:12,480
那他肯定也掏得起那张40英镑的罚单，
And he should be able
to pay the £40 ticket he got

255
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:17,160
罚款原因是他没把车停在车位框里——
而那个框根本就没那辆车宽。
for not parking it within the box which
wasn't wide enough for the car.

256
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:19,200
车位框难道不应该画得
Shouldn't the box be wide enough

257
00:14:19,240 --> 00:14:20,960
比车宽吗？这才是正常逻辑吧。
for a car? It would make sense.

258
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,880
哈，他还算走运的，前几天我也吃了张罚单，
Yeah, he's lucky,
I got a ticket the other day,

259
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:25,880
没跟你们开玩笑，理由居然是“停车姿势太差”。
and I kid you not, for being parked badly.

260
00:14:25,920 --> 00:14:27,400
[观众轻笑]
[AUDIENCE CHUCKLING]

261
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:29,640
停车这事儿什么时候搞得跟花样滑冰一样了？
Since when did it become like ice-skating?

262
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:32,440
一个个裁判似地杵在那儿……
“啧，我觉得这车停得不够优美。”
All standing there...
"No, I don't think that is well parked."

263
00:14:32,480 --> 00:14:35,000
尼日利亚裁判只给了三分。
Only three from the Nigerian judge.

264
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,520
[笑声]
[LAUGHTER]

265
00:14:36,560 --> 00:14:38,240
而且这种机制也太消极了，
And that's kind of negative as well,

266
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:39,840
真要这么干，总得胡萝卜加大棒兼备吧。
if they're gonna do that,
it's gotta be carrot and stick.

267
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:42,200
他们也得来点正向激励，
So they need to do something positive

